=== completion
--- pathed 
add 	add directories (at the front)
clean 	normalise PATH: absolute, no duplicates or empty entries
edit 	edit PATH in $VISUAL or $EDITOR
help 	show the usage
list 	PATH, numbered, with notes
mv 	move an entry
rm 	remove entries
undo 	undo the last change
which 	every copy of a command in PATH
--- pathed add -
--after=	add after an entry
--before=	add before an entry
-a 	add at the end
-f 	add directories that don't exist
-m 	move directories that are already in PATH
-n 	show what would change, without changing PATH
-v 	show what changed
--- pathed add --before 
~/one 	1
~/two 	2
--- pathed add n
new/
--- pathed rm 
~/one 	1
~/two 	2
--- pathed rm 1
1 	~/one
--- pathed rm ~/
~/one 	1
~/two 	2
--- pathed mv 1 
1 	~/one
2 	~/two
3 	''
4 	~/one
first 	the front of PATH
last 	the end of PATH
--- pathed undo -
-f 	undo even if PATH has changed since, not by pathed
-l 	list the changes that can be undone, the last first
-n 	show what would change, without changing PATH
--- pathed which to
tool 
